  "summary": "In this white paper, we highlight the importance of the ($1-10~{\\rm Hz}$) frequency range for laboratory tests of the quantum nature of gravity using the quantum gravity-induced entanglement of masses (QGEM) protocol. QGEM requires matter-wave interferometers with masses ($m\\sim10^{-15}-10^{-14}~{\\rm kg}$), brought within separations ($d\\sim30-50~μ{\\rm m}$), while maintaining spatial superpositions of ($1-20~μ{\\rm m}$) and coherence for ($τ\\sim 0.1 - 1~{\\rm s}$). These requirements make low-frequency environmental noise a central experimental challenge and place QGEM in a regime closely…",
